# Build context exclusions.
#
# Every Dockerfile here does `COPY . .`, so without this file the context is the
# entire working tree — .git history, a 4 GB engine-database directory,
# node_modules, the Python venv. That is slow, and worse it makes the layer
# cache useless: touching any ignored file invalidates the COPY layer and forces
# a full rebuild of eight images.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT MUST NOT BE EXCLUDED, and why
#
#   go.mod, go.sum      the dependency layer
#   migrations/**       EMBEDDED via go:embed in migrations/embed.go. Excluding
#                       these fails the BUILD, not the run — go:embed cannot
#                       find the pattern and the compile errors.
#   docs/reference/     the CERT-In profile YAML, read at runtime
#   OSINT/              tools.manifest.yaml, read at runtime by the workers
#
# Anything added under a go:embed pattern in future must be checked against
# this list.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Version control
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Secrets — never bake an env file into an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python
.venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
*.egg-info

# Node — the frontend image runs its own npm ci
node_modules
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist

# Go build artefacts
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Downloaded scanner binaries and provisioned engine databases (multi-GB).
# These are mounted at runtime, never built in.
.axebom
enginedb

# Local state
*.log
tmp/
.idea
.vscode

# Test fixtures are large and only used by the test suite, which does not run
# inside these images. The GOLDEN CORPUS stays out of production images.
fixtures

# Documentation, except the reference data that is read at runtime.
docs/phases
docs/ADR
docs/*.md

# Deployment descriptors do not belong inside the images they describe
deploy/compose
deploy/k8s
perf
